Problem 3:
hell yea the function worked, so i'll explain it here:
the problem i was having was that the sigmas were a tuple of how many passes to do with possibly 
differing values. I handled it like this:
at the beginning of the function, i have an if statement that asks if len(sigmas) == 0: return mask.
(mask being the bool array of true / false for data to include). the first round wont have the len as 0,
so it goes through modifying WHERE the values are greater than n*sigma, sets those as false.
it then returns itself, return sigrej(data, sigmas[1:], mask) now including the bad values. sigmas will now have
one less indicies than it did before. This happens until all the len is 0, and all of the runs have happened,
then returning the mask it was called with.

